    "result_text": "The test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule \"reject creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by any other owner, responding 409\" by adding a new step to the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline, following the same pattern already used for the telephone/household uniqueness checks:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** \u2014 the check function. It reads the validated request (whose email `ValidateNewOwner` already lower-cases via `OwnerEmail.normalize`), skips when no email was supplied, and throws `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` if any existing owner's lower-cased email matches.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause).\n\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict`.\n\n4. **`...DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml`** (escalation) \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `checkEmailUnique` step between `checkTelephoneUnique` and `checkHouseholdUnique`, under the same `transaction` governance, so a duplicate is rejected before anything is persisted.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` now passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
